//
// PROBE: bund.exit and its alias exit (Bund/src/stdlib/functions/bund/bund_exit.rs:10-31,
// Bund/src/stdlib/functions/create_aliases.rs:31).
//
// exit ends the program where it stands: the rest of the lambda, the rest of
// the program, and the capture's own epilogue never run. In Bund2 it is a
// request the embedder honours (D52).
//
"probe: exit inside a word stops everything after it" println
:f { "inside, before exit" println 3 exit "inside, after exit" println } register
"before the call" println
f
"after the call" println
